Fix the vertical crop of the footer wordmark introduced by PR #5264 (DIG-2290 review finding #5).

## The defect

`apps/digithings-web/app/globals.css` changed `.pixel-word-band`:

```diff
 .pixel-word-band {
-  padding: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem) var(--page-pad) 0;
-  overflow-x: clip;
+  display: flex;
+  justify-content: center;
+  align-items: center;
+  height: clamp(4.5rem, 12vw, 9rem);
+  padding-left: var(--page-pad);
+  padding-right: var(--page-pad);
+  overflow: clip;
 }
```

`overflow-x: clip` became `overflow: clip`, and the band gained a fixed height with `align-items: center`. The wordmark (`PixelWordmark` footer variant, `viewBox="0 0 88 10"`, aspect 8.8) is now clipped on **both** axes against a fixed height, shaving pixels off the top and bottom rows of every glyph.

Measured in Chrome at the real CSS values:

| viewport | crop | % of mark height | pixel rows lost |
|---|---|---|---|
| 1280 | 0 | 0% | 0 |
| 1440 | 7.8 px | 5.1% | ~0.5 |
| 1600 | 26.0 px | 15.3% | ~1.5 |
| 1728 | 37.8 px | 20.8% | ~2.1 |

Develop crops nothing at any width. It reads as the wordmark being squashed: the `D` loses its notched corners, the `I` loses its serif rows.

